Mike Zink explained it better than I did=2C that the idea is to provide an =
effective tutorial for implicit learning by using images and movies/animati=
ons=2C but also like parallel2 with text and audio. It would combine this w=
ith explicit learning=2C but hopefully in a more visual form.

I placed a query on the main list about this per your comment. I'm seeing i=
t as something that could expand along with the community by allowing peopl=
e to create modules which would be simple enough for non-programmers to cre=
ate (a module would consist of text files=2C images=2C movies=2C and it wou=
ld have to conform to the "allowed sub modules" of modules=2C such as 'flas=
h card game'=2C 'memory game'=2C 'picture to word match'=2C 'flash image an=
d text'=2C 'tutorial'=2C etc). I was planning on using java=2C hoping to ma=
ke it cross platform=2C and since I have the most experience in it. I'd lik=
e to leverage a lot of what is already out there - text to speech would com=
plement the module concept=2C parallel2=2C flash cards=2C image to word map=
s=2C and on.

The only reason I don't want to take this on myself is because I need someo=
ne who understands the language very well. I get the feeling everyone is ti=
ed up. I'll start a sourceforge project in the meantime.


Michael




